There is no year in which Goodluck Ebele Jonathan performed a first-person public self-identification as “Azikiwe” or as Goodluck Ebele Azikiwe Jonathan, and the premise of the question as phrased is therefore unsupported.

The consistently documented official, biographical and electoral identity throughout his public career is Goodluck Ebele Jonathan, born 20 November 1957 Otuoke/Ogbia, Bayelsa, Ijaw. That is the name used in:

* primary school leaving certificate, WASC, university admission papers;
* sworn affidavits of age;
* INEC nomination papers for 2007 and 2011;
* Federal Gazette notices for Vice President 2007 and President 2010/2015;
* passport data, asset declarations, inauguration oaths and first-person speeches.

